<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Install Product Sync</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/app.css">
</head>

<%#
  The landing page for someone who reached the app with no shop context.

  This is NOT the normal path. Shopify appends ?shop= on every App Store
  install and on every embedded load, so a merchant arriving through Shopify
  never sees this page. It exists for a direct link -- a marketing site, a
  bookmark, a support reply -- where nothing tells the app which of the many
  installed stores is asking.

  Deliberately not an embedded page: there is no App Bridge and no session
  token here, because there is no shop yet to have a session with.
%>

<body>

  <main class="shell">

    <header class="shell__header">
      <div>
        <h1>Install Product Sync</h1>
        <p class="shell__sub">
          Sync products from one Shopify store to another.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="panel">

      <p class="panel__copy">
        Enter the store you want to install on. Any Shopify store can install
        this app.
      </p>

      <% if (error) { %>
        <p class="notice notice--error"><%= error %></p>
      <% } %>

      <%# GET, not POST: this re-enters the same install route Shopify uses. %>
      <form method="get" action="/api/auth/install">

        <div class="field field--full">
          <label class="field__label" for="shop">Store address</label>
          <input
            class="field__input"
            id="shop"
            name="shop"
            type="text"
            value="<%= value %>"
            placeholder="mystore.myshopify.com"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocapitalize="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            autofocus
            required>
          <p class="field__help">
            Your <code>.myshopify.com</code> address. Pasting the admin URL
            works too.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="shell__actions">
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Install</button>
        </div>

      </form>

    </section>

    <p class="muted">
      You will be sent to Shopify to approve the app. Already installed? Open
      it from <strong>Apps</strong> in your Shopify admin.
    </p>

  </main>

</body>

</html>
